<!--
  Status-bar notification icon.

  capacitor.config.json has named `ic_stat_icon` as the LocalNotifications
  smallIcon since the daily reminder was added, and no such drawable existed —
  Android fell back to the launcher icon, which it then renders as a white
  silhouette of a full-colour square. FCM is stricter: naming a missing drawable
  in the manifest is a build error, so it had to exist before push could ship.

  Android masks this to a single colour and ignores everything but the alpha
  channel, so it is drawn as a flat white leaf on transparency. Anything with
  interior detail or a background disappears into a white blob at 24dp.
-->
